om\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Viktor</a>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   423→                        AI coworker that lives in Slack and automates workflows by observing team behavior. Proactively suggests automations and runs autonomously without manual setup.\n   424→                    </div>\n   425→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   426→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   427→                        <span>Product Hunt</span>\n   428→                    </div>\n   429→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"An AI coworker that actually does the work\"</div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"meta\">Released: 2026-04-01</div>\n   431→                </div>\n   432→\n   433→                <div class=\"item\">\n   434→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   435→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/future-agi/traceAI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">traceAI</a>\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   438→                        Open-source LLM tracing framework designed specifically for GenAI applications. Captures every LLM call, prompt, token count, retrieval step, and agent decision.\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   441→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   442→                        <span>GitHub</span>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Open-source LLM tracing that speaks GenAI, not HTTP\"</div>\n   445→                    <div class=\"meta\">Released: 2026-04-01</div>\n   446→                </div>\n   447→\n   448→                <div class=\"item\">\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   450→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anton-abyzov/ccx-rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CCX-RS</a>\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   453→                        Community Claude Code eXtended — free, open-source AI coding assistant in Rust. Features 19 tools, multi-model support, and Claude Code-style TUI interface.\n   454→                    </div>\n   455→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   456→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source AI coding agent</span>\n   457→                        <span>GitHub</span>\n   458→                    </div>\n   459→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"19 tools, multi-model, Claude Code-style TUI\"</div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"meta\">Released: 2026-03-31</div>\n   461→                </div>\n   462→\n   463→                <div class=\"item\">\n   464→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   465→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/baton-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Baton</a>\n   466→                    </div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   468→                        Desktop app for developing with AI coding agents. Run multiple agents in parallel, each in their own git-isolated workspace. Provides PR-ready code review.\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   471→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   472→                        <span>Product Hunt</span>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"meta\">Released: 2026-03-30</div>\n   475→                </div>\n   476→\n   477→                <div class=\"item\">\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   479→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/NiuTrans/ToFu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ToFu</a>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   482→                        Self-hosted AI assistant with tool use, multi-agent orchestration, and coding copilot. Lightweight Flask + vanilla JS stack for complete self-hosted solution.\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   485→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source AI coding agent</span>\n   486→                        <span>GitHub</span>\n   487→                    </div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"meta\">Released: 2026-03-30</div>\n   489→                </div>\n   490→            </section>\n   491→\n   492→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   493→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   494→                <h2>Product Updates (12)</h2>\n   495→\n   496→                <div class=\"item\">\n   497→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   498→                        <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.101</span>\n   499→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code</a>\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   502→                        Added /team-onboarding command, OS CA certificate trust, interactive Google Vertex AI setup, faster diff computation, and reduced memory usage.\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   505→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   506→                        <span>2026-04-10</span>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                </div>\n   509→\n   510→                <div class=\"item\">\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   512→                        <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.98</span>\n   513→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code</a>\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→                    <div class=